From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:58:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdnsp-sky1: drop the shutdown hook that takes down the
 PCIe x1 links

On the Minisforum MS-R1, asserting the cdnsp-sky1 controller resets (and
gating its SCMI clocks) from ->shutdown() drops both PCIe x1 links: the
x1 root ports report an LTSSM transition to DETECT_QUIET and PHY errors
right after the USB controllers enter reset. device_shutdown() then reaches
r8169, whose shutdown reads the RTL8127 behind the dead link. The read
either completes with an error, giving an asynchronous SError and a panic,
or never completes, leaving the CPU stalled on the bus (no response even to
a pseudo-NMI) until someone power-cycles the board. Every reboot of the
board ended one of those two ways; keeping the clocks on and only asserting
the resets did not change that.

The xHCI shutdown has already halted the controller and its DMA by the time
the glue's hook would run, and firmware resets the SoC on reboot, so the
hook does nothing a reboot needs. Remove it. With it gone, two consecutive
reboots reach "reboot: Restarting system" with both links up to the end.

Signed-off-by: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c | 14 --------------
 1 file changed, 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
index 2c42db17f..49ab3976a 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -875,19 +875,6 @@ static const struct acpi_device_id cdnsp_sky1_acpi_match[] = {
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(acpi, cdnsp_sky1_acpi_match);
 
-static void cdnsp_sky1_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
-{
-	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
-	struct cdnsp_sky1 *data = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-
-	if (!device_may_wakeup(dev)) {
-		dev_dbg(dev, "at %s, reset controller\n", __func__);
-		reset_control_assert(data->reset);
-		reset_control_assert(data->preset);
-		sky1_usb_clk_disable_all(dev);
-	}
-}
-
 static struct platform_driver cdnsp_sky1_driver = {
 	.probe		= cdnsp_sky1_probe,
 	.remove		= cdnsp_sky1_remove,
@@ -897,7 +884,6 @@ static struct platform_driver cdnsp_sky1_driver = {
 		.acpi_match_table = ACPI_PTR(cdnsp_sky1_acpi_match),
 		.pm	= &cdnsp_sky1_pm_ops,
 	},
-	.shutdown = cdnsp_sky1_shutdown,
 };
 
 module_platform_driver(cdnsp_sky1_driver);
-- 
